WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
- How are you?

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.960
- [Kelly] I'm so--
- We've never met.

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:03.140
- I know. And it's so crazy.

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:04.487
I was literally backstage going,

00:00:04.487 --> 00:00:05.740
"Wait, I've never met her."

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:06.820
- [Ava] I've never met you.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:07.900
- You're so badass!

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:08.940
- Oh, thank you.
- Yeah! (audience cheering)

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.380
- As are you, as are you.
(audience cheering)

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:11.340
- [Kelly] I, incredibly--
- Thank you.

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:13.480
- [Kelly] I feel like
I'm a very busy woman

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.928
but I feel like you have upped me,

00:00:14.928 --> 00:00:15.761
(Ava laughing)

00:00:15.761 --> 00:00:16.830
you are like far busier than me.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:18.680
- Busy but blessed.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:19.890
They call it booked and busy--

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.083
- [Kelly] Booked and blessed.
- And blessed.

00:00:21.083 --> 00:00:22.199
- [Kelly] That has all
the B's. - [Ava] Yes.

00:00:22.199 --> 00:00:23.032
- I love that--

00:00:23.032 --> 00:00:23.865
- All the B's!

00:00:23.865 --> 00:00:24.698
(audience clapping)
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:00:24.698 --> 00:00:25.540
Um, well, you're so busy

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.070
as I said that even Shonda Rhimes

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:28.390
gave you some great advice.

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:29.223
- [Kelly] What was that?

00:00:29.223 --> 00:00:30.130
- She did. I called her

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:30.963
and I said, "You know,

00:00:30.963 --> 00:00:31.847
"you've got so much going on.

00:00:31.847 --> 00:00:32.957
"I've got a lot going on

00:00:32.957 --> 00:00:34.647
"but you seem to be a
little calmer than me,

00:00:34.647 --> 00:00:35.480
"how do you do it?"
- [Kelly] More balanced?

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:36.347
- A little more balanced.

00:00:36.347 --> 00:00:37.270
"What are you doing?"

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.103
And she said,

00:00:38.103 --> 00:00:39.000
"Oh, well, do you work on the weekend?"

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.097
And I said, "Well, yeah,

00:00:40.097 --> 00:00:41.090
"definitely work on the weekend."

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:41.923
And she said,

00:00:41.923 --> 00:00:42.756
"Do you ever get caught up?"

00:00:42.756 --> 00:00:44.407
And I was like, "Yeah, no,

00:00:44.407 --> 00:00:45.387
"I never get caught up

00:00:45.387 --> 00:00:46.567
"where I work on the weekend." She said,

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:48.260
"So, then stop doing it.
Why are you doing it?"

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.093
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:49.093 --> 00:00:50.120
- And so it just really made me,

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.110
help me reprioritize my time.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:52.943
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:52.943 --> 00:00:53.850
You know what helped me is kids.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.290
Like, it's like I want to be a great mom.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:56.270
And mine was like,

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:58.680
my kids I'm like, that my
daughter will shame me.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.780
My seven-year-old has
some shame game, y'all.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:01.613
Like, she'll be like,

00:01:01.613 --> 00:01:02.450
"Why are you on your phone?"
(Ava laughing)

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:03.890
And I'll be like, "I'm not."

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:04.970
And I'll put it down. Like,
(Ava laughing)

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:06.570
so, I stopped doing weekend stuff.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:07.650
Like, I try my best

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.012
every once in a while something pops up--

00:01:09.012 --> 00:01:09.845
- [Ava] Yeah.

00:01:09.845 --> 00:01:11.490
- And shame game comes to cry to me.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:12.840
But it's hard though to stop--

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:13.860
- [Ava] It is.
- When you love what you do.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:14.920
- [Ava] When you love
what you do-- - Yeah.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:15.760
- [Ava] You know? And it's, it's,

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:17.380
it's a part of making films

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:18.723
and telling stories is,

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:21.480
you know, a beautiful part of my life.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:23.230
So, to say, "I have to stop at this time,"

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:24.537
it's something that I've not done, but--

00:01:24.537 --> 00:01:25.950
- [Kelly] But you're a creator. - Yeah.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:27.159
- [Kelly] It's hard to
just be like-- - I love it.

00:01:27.159 --> 00:01:27.992
- [Kelly] Like, I'm not gonna to create--

00:01:27.992 --> 00:01:28.825
- [Ava] That's--
- Over the weekends.

00:01:28.825 --> 00:01:30.480
- [Ava] That's right. - We
should probably listen to her.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:32.040
Um, so yeah, "Balance is good,"

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.540
so my therapist says. Um,

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.700
so were you always so good at,

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:36.710
dedicated to work?

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:37.543
Like, even back,

00:01:37.543 --> 00:01:38.376
I heard that you,

00:01:38.376 --> 00:01:39.209
we were both waitresses.

00:01:39.209 --> 00:01:40.110
I was a waitress as well before--

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:40.943
- [Ava] Yeah.

00:01:40.943 --> 00:01:41.776
- I feel like all of us were waitresses.

00:01:41.776 --> 00:01:42.760
- [Ava] Yeah.
- I loved it.

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:44.020
- [Ava] I loved it and I was really good.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:45.400
- [Kelly] I was good.
- I was good.

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:47.410
- [Kelly] Yeah. I knew how
to really use first names,

00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:48.243
get a better tip.

00:01:48.243 --> 00:01:49.139
- [Ava] Oh, what you're say--
- Yeah--

00:01:49.139 --> 00:01:50.210
- [Ava] What you're saying--
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.330
- Just feel out what they want:

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:52.740
Do they want more
conversation? - [Kelly] Yes.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:53.573
- Do they want more space?

00:01:53.573 --> 00:01:54.470
- Yes!

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:56.330
- All the little extra things you'd bring.

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:57.163
Yes.

00:01:57.163 --> 00:01:58.300
I knew who to target in the family.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:01:59.740
- [Kelly] Yes!
- You like pull out the...

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:00.740
I was so good at--
- [Kelly] That's a talent.

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:01.890
- It is. And I always think,

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:03.380
if this Hollywood thing goes wrong

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:04.690
and I can't make movies anymore--

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:05.523
- [Kelly] Yup.
- I'll be fine.

00:02:05.523 --> 00:02:06.450
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:07.520
- [Kelly] 'Cause I'm a killer waitress.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:08.410
- [Ava] Yeah, I'm a killer waitress.

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:09.810
- Me too. I'm personable--

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:10.643
- I can tell you were good,

00:02:10.643 --> 00:02:11.476
I mean, I can--
- I'm just saying--

00:02:11.476 --> 00:02:12.701
- Just imagine her coming to your table--

00:02:12.701 --> 00:02:13.534
- Yeah.

00:02:13.534 --> 00:02:14.367
- Taking a order.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.200
- You would probably want me to leave:

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.033
I like to talk.
(Ava laughing)

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:16.866
Um, but I would say,
(audience laughing)

00:02:16.866 --> 00:02:17.699
I would say, I was like,

00:02:17.699 --> 00:02:19.060
"I don't think you like a talker."

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:20.034
So, I'd walk away
- [Ava] Right!

00:02:20.034 --> 00:02:22.096
- And then I'd use it
all on the other table.

00:02:22.096 --> 00:02:23.900
But um, did, I heard, um,

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:25.390
did you ever see Little Richard?

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:26.223
Did you wait on like,

00:02:26.223 --> 00:02:27.056
you waited on people
- [Ava] Yeah.

00:02:27.056 --> 00:02:28.334
I did not wait on people like that.

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:29.840
- Yeah. I worked at a place
called Aunt Kizzy's Back Porch

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:30.750
in LA.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.950
And on Sundays they had
a very famous brunch

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:35.610
where a lot of people
would come - known people.

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:37.250
- [Kelly] Yeah. - Little
Richard came every Sunday.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:38.570
I was at UCLA at the time

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:39.403
as a student
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:39.403 --> 00:02:40.236
working.

00:02:40.236 --> 00:02:41.590
And he left me a $100 tip

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:43.180
on a $60 cheque.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:44.013
- [Kelly] Wow.

00:02:44.013 --> 00:02:44.990
- [Ava] Every Sunday.

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:46.920
He really put me through
college, basically.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:47.807
- [Kelly] Wait, so--

00:02:47.807 --> 00:02:48.640
- Yeah.
(audience clapping)

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:49.473
- [Kelly] Are you this person now?

00:02:49.473 --> 00:02:51.107
I promised myself as a waitress...

00:02:51.107 --> 00:02:53.100
'Cause people would surprise
me with tips like that,

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.817
and I was like, "Man,
if I ever make it, like,

00:02:54.817 --> 00:02:55.737
"if I make some money

00:02:55.737 --> 00:02:56.690
"in life,"

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:57.927
I was like, I'm always gonna like--

00:02:57.927 --> 00:02:58.760
- [Ava] I'm a great tipper.
- Like, surprise...

00:02:58.760 --> 00:02:59.870
- Are you? I'm a great--

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:00.830
- That's what I'm saying.
- Yes!

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:01.663
You know why?

00:03:01.663 --> 00:03:03.340
Because people don't
realize you are hustling.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:04.173
- [Ava] You're livin' on it, yeah.

00:03:04.173 --> 00:03:05.006
- Yeah.
- Absolutely.

00:03:05.006 --> 00:03:06.870
- [Kelly] Yeah. And
everybody comes at once.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:07.703
You get slammed.

00:03:07.703 --> 00:03:09.170
It's not like it's spread
out during the day.

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:11.426
Just everyone wants to
eat all day, all hours.

00:03:11.426 --> 00:03:13.040
(Ava laughing)
It's like you're slammed.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:13.900
Anyway. I tip well.

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:14.914
That's really cool that you do that, yeah.

00:03:14.914 --> 00:03:16.082
- [Ava] Well, it's important
that you do it if you can.

00:03:16.082 --> 00:03:16.915
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:16.915 --> 00:03:18.070
- You know so, yeah.
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:20.320
Well, um speaking of
music, uh, Little Richard,

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:21.690
Um, who is your favorite band to see

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:22.670
if I always like to ask,

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:24.440
who do you love to see, like, live?

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:25.273
- [Kelly] Who's your band?

00:03:25.273 --> 00:03:26.106
- U2.

00:03:26.106 --> 00:03:26.939
- [Kelly] Oh, good! Really?

00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:28.018
- Yes. And when I came into

00:03:28.018 --> 00:03:30.694
your beautiful dressing
rooms in the back...

00:03:30.694 --> 00:03:34.530
You have, she has albums
on each of the room--

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:35.363
- [Kelly] Vinyl, yeah.

00:03:35.363 --> 00:03:36.640
- Vinyl albums on each of the rooms.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.070
And I walked in and there was a U2 album.

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:39.820
I said, "Oh, they did this for me."

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.230
And they were like, "No, this is--

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:42.930
- [Kelly] That's one
of my favorite records.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:43.890
Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:44.723
- [Ava] I love them.

00:03:44.723 --> 00:03:46.310
I've seen them over 30 times in concerts.

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:48.090
- [Kelly] Oh, my God.
- Since I was 18 years old.

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:49.520
- [Kelly] Wow.
- They're just like my,

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:51.250
my Bible of a band.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.220
- [Kelly] You know, it's
funny you said Bible.

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:53.190
I was literally about to say,

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:54.100
I saw them live

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:55.655
and it was like a spiritual experience.

00:03:55.655 --> 00:03:56.830
- [Ava] Mm, yeah.
- Like, it was,

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:58.330
it was bigger than just music

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:00.140
and it was so, like, connecting,

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:01.670
like, you would, none
of us knew each other

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:02.650
and the audience, you know--
- [Ava] Yeah.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:04.470
- We're all just like
experiencing the same thing.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:06.800
It's such a beautifully... I'm
so glad live music is back.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.290
But yeah, wow.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:10.210
- [Ava] I think it's because
their music is about something,

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:11.043
it has meaning.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:11.043 --> 00:04:12.680
- And so, it kind of, yeah, it kind of.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:13.513
- [Kelly] What's your favorite song?

00:04:13.513 --> 00:04:14.346
I'm just curious.

00:04:14.346 --> 00:04:15.802
- [Ava] It's so impossible to,

00:04:15.802 --> 00:04:16.950
for me to choose.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:17.930
I'd probably say

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:18.763
probably "One".

00:04:18.763 --> 00:04:20.390
One of my favorites.
- [Kelly] Oh, God!

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:22.200
- One of my favorites.
- When he did it with Mary J.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.033
- [Ava] I know.
- [Kelly] God!

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:24.570
- Now it's just another level.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:25.560
Yeah, there's so many great songs.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:27.730
- Yes. You should sing that.
- Okay. I, being I--

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:28.710
- I'm making a request.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:29.730
- [Kelly] Sometimes I get nervous

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:31.010
about covering certain songs

00:04:31.010 --> 00:04:31.843
and then sometimes I'm like,

00:04:31.843 --> 00:04:33.210
"Oh, I shouldn't have covered that."

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:34.453
Um, but I did it.

